here  black america was at that time it's a  beautiful film with a lot to say  and it's funny and cool too  favorite comfort film for me is eternal  sunshine of the spotless mind  i i'm sorry i just said hi  jim carrey after a breakup with kate  winslet's character  um tries to erase her from his memories  you know it doesn't shy away from like  the big bold sad  feelings of a breakup as the movie goes  on  there's such humor in it and every time  i watch it it just  swells my heart the name's bond  james bond it's casino royale it's the  the daniel craig's first outing as as  james bond i just there's something  about that movie i just  absolutely love the action in it is so  great but the world is so great and  they're off in montenegro and  in tuxedos and they're playing card  games and people are drinking martinis  and eating caviar  and i just think it's the perfect escape  the acting's amazing in it  the opening sequence is one of the  greatest action sequences you'll ever  see and daniel craig is  is his bond as far as i'm concerned i  pick a recent movie man uh and that  would be  either avengers infinity uh war or  avengers end game  this is the fight of our lives if i got  nothing new to watch  i will make a meal and sit down and  start watching  end game all over again and stuff so  those marvel movies are my  they're my happy places my grandmother  used to refer to uh the soap opera she  would watch those are my stories  those marvel movies and story so that's  my comfort food those are the movies i  go to to feel embraced and warm  when he was out there fighting i was  here  [Music]  holding that bar day and night  you know a great movie for the times  that we're in um is a little known film  um in some circles it's called ashes and  embers  it is a film that traces the  homecoming of a black vietnam veteran it  came out in the 80s  um and it's talking about the black  soldiers who came back from vietnam  but it really is talking about the  condition of